cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TRIAD, please cite it with the data in this file."
title: "TRIAD: Trusted RDF Interoperable Agent Data"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Asish A.
    family-names: George
    affiliation: University of Victoria
  - given-names: Mohamed Khaled
    family-names: Abuela
    affiliation: University of Victoria
repository-code: "https://github.com/MohamedKhalidmk/TRIAD"
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
abstract: >-
  A data model for clinical records that many people make and change over time.
  Each clinical fact is an assertion with an author and a source, and a new assertion
  supersedes the old one, so the current state is the result of a traversal.
  The Milestone 4 prototype is a hospital web app on SQLite with a Care Assistant chat.
  The clinical entities follow HL7 FHIR R4. All data is synthetic (Synthea).
keywords:
  - clinical records
  - provenance
  - HL7 FHIR
  - relational database
  - SQLite
